s and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":25},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":11,"html":12,"skills":13,"hooks":17,"files":18,"sources":22},"npm-audit-fix","skill","Clear npm audit findings per sub-project, honor allowlists, verify with project scripts, open one PR per sub-project.",[6,7,8,9,10],"npm","audit","security","dependencies","vulnerabilities","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The skill clears \u003Ccode>npm audit\u003C/code> findings in every Node sub-project of a repo, one sub-project at a time. It fixes what it can, verifies with the project&#39;s own scripts, and opens one PR per sub-project. Findings that would break the build or that you allowlisted stay out of the PR and are listed in its body.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Fix npm audit issues&quot; or &quot;fix the vulnerability alerts&quot;.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>A monorepo with several \u003Ccode>package-lock.json\u003C/code> files that each need their own PR.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Runs \u003Ccode>npm audit fix\u003C/code>, then pins direct deps or adds \u003Ccode>overrides\u003C/code> for transitive ones.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Verifies with whichever of \u003Ccode>format\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>check\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>typecheck\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>lint\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>build\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>test\u003C/code> the project defines, and rolls back a bump that breaks them.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Reads skips from your request, a \u003Ccode>.claude/audit-allowlist.json\u003C/code>, or the project&#39;s CLAUDE.md. It never uses \u003Ccode>--force\u003C/code> or a fake downgrade to clear an allowlisted advisory.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Opens \u003Ccode>chore/npm-audit-&lt;sub-project&gt;\u003C/code> branches with a short PR body: patched, upgraded, allowlisted, deferred.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>npm\u003C/code> and the GitHub CLI (\u003Ccode>gh\u003C/code>), authenticated.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[14],{"name":2,"description":15,"argumentHint":-1,"invocation":16},"Use when the user asks to fix npm audit vulnerabilities, npm audit issues, or vulnerability issues. Walks each Node sub-project, patches what it can, respects per-project allowlists, opens one PR per sub-project.","/npm-audit-fix:npm-audit-fix",[],[19,20,21],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","skills/npm-audit-fix/SKILL.md",[23],{"path":21,"html":24},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">npm-audit-fix\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">description\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">Use when the user asks to fix npm audit vulnerabilities, npm audit issues, or vulnerability issues. Walks each Node sub-project, patches what it can, respects per-project allowlists, opens one PR per sub-project.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"># npm audit fix\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Patch npm vulnerabilities. One PR per sub-project, never bundled.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## When to use\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> \"fix npm audit issues\" / \"fix vulnerability issues\" / \"fix npm audit vulns\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Any variant where the user wants \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`npm audit`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> findings cleared\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Allowlist\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Some bumps must be skipped because they break a working dependency or have no real upstream fix. Sources, in order:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">1.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> The user's request in the current conversation.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">2.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> A \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`.claude/audit-allowlist.json`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (or similar) in the sub-project or workspace root, if present.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">3.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> The sub-project's CLAUDE.md if it documents one.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Once a skip is established from one of these, apply it without asking. If none of them mention a skip and a bump fails the project's verify step, that finding goes in \"Deferred\". Do not force it through.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">A typical allowlist entry is an advisory where npm's only proposed fix is a bogus downgrade of a parent package (for example to a \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`0.0.x`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> release). Do not add an override or any other workaround to clear it.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">When the only remaining advisories after \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`npm audit fix`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> are allowlisted, stop. Do not override, downgrade, or \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`--force`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">. Report them as allowlisted in the PR body and move on.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Phase 0: Scope\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">1.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Workspace root: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">2.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> In-scope sub-projects:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">   -\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> cwd is the workspace root: every dir containing both \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`package.json`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> and \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`package-lock.json`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (use \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`find -maxdepth 4 -name package-lock.json -not -path '*/node_modules/*'`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"